# Allowlist, not denylist (S-01).
#
# The denylist that used to live here failed exactly the way denylists fail:
# `vsce ls` showed the package would ship scripts/aws/*.ps1 (a personal email
# and AWS resource names), scripts/vm-*.cmd (the lab VM's IP and paths),
# out-integration/*.js (the built test harness) and raw TypeScript sources —
# none of which the extension needs to run. Every new folder added to the repo
# would have had to be remembered here, forever.
#
# So: exclude everything, then add back only what is loaded at runtime. A new
# folder is now invisible to the package by default.
#
# Verify after ANY change with:  npx @vscode/vsce ls

**

# --- required by the Marketplace ---
!package.json
!README.md
!LICENSE.md
!CHANGELOG.md
# Third-party notices: EULA section 5.4 promises this ships WITH the extension,
# not just in the repo, so a customer can read it without network access.
!NOTICES.md

# --- loaded at runtime ---
# Named precisely, never with a folder wildcard: in vsce a `!` rule always wins
# over every exclusion regardless of order, so `!dist/webview/**` would re-include
# the .map files permanently and no later rule could take them back out. Source
# maps re-expose the whole source and add ~5 MB.
!dist/extension.js
!dist/mcp-server.js
!dist/webview/*.js
!media/icon.png
!media/icon.svg
!media/walkthrough/*.md
!snippets/*.json
